 ## How it works
-The method permutes the 3-bit level codes within a Morton code based on the signs of the ray direction components $(x, y, z)$. This ensures that when voxels are sorted by their mapped Morton codes, they appear in the correct back-to-front order for volume rendering or rasterization.
